/-!
# The cyclotomic auxiliary field of prime conductor `q`

This file proves `NK.CFTLib.IdeleHasse.Crux.cyclotomicAuxiliary`.  The auxiliary field
`M = K(ζ_q)` is realised as the intermediate field `K⟮ζ_q⟯` inside `E := CyclotomicField q L`
(the cyclotomic field of conductor `q` over `L`), so that all the required algebra structures are
the canonical ones.  The compositum property `E = L·M` is the statement that `L` and `ζ_q`
generate `E` over `K`, and `E/K` is Galois because `E/K` is generated by the Galois extension
`L/K` and the cyclotomic (hence Galois) subextension `M/K`.

The number-theoretic content is the divisibility of the inertia degree: at a prime `w` of `M`
above `Q`, the residue field `𝓞 M ⧸ w` contains the image of a primitive `q`-th root of unity
(integral over `𝓞 K`), which therefore has order exactly `q`; hence `q ∣ #(𝓞 M ⧸ w) - 1`.
Since `#(𝓞 M ⧸ w) = NQ ^ f(w|Q)` and `q ∤ NQ`, this gives `ord_q(NQ) ∣ f(w|Q)`.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
set_option linter.unusedVariables false
set_option linter.style.haveILetI false
set_option maxHeartbeats 800000

